My Australian Concise Oxford (1st Ed - 1987) differs:

agnostic n & a. (adherent) of the view that nothing is known, or 
likely to be known, of the existence of God or of anything beyond 
material phenomena.

atheism n. disbelief in the existence of God or gods; godlessness; 
so ~ist.

Note the first is phrased in terms of knowledge, the second in 
terms of belief. A statement is true or false (or paradoxical*, 
inconsistent etc). A belief about a statement, or the content of a 
statement, can be towards the statement being true, towards it 
being false, or neutral [I believe, I believe not, I do not 
believe].

"This statement is false."

